# Styling and Design Guidelines

## Tailwind CSS Usage
- Use Tailwind CSS utility classes for styling
- Follow mobile-first responsive design
- Use consistent spacing scale (4, 8, 12, 16, 24, 32px)
- Use semantic color names from Tailwind palette

## Dark Mode Support
- Always include dark mode variants with `dark:` prefix
- Use consistent dark mode color scheme
- Test components in both light and dark themes
- Use CSS variables for theme switching

## Color Palette
- **Primary**: Blue (blue-600, blue-700, blue-800)
- **Secondary**: Gray (gray-100 to gray-900)
- **Success**: Green (green-500, green-600)
- **Warning**: Yellow (yellow-500, yellow-600)
- **Error**: Red (red-500, red-600)
- **Info**: Blue (blue-500, blue-600)

## Typography
- Use Inter font family (configured in layout)
- Heading hierarchy: h1 (text-3xl), h2 (text-2xl), h3 (text-xl)
- Body text: text-base (16px)
- Small text: text-sm (14px)
- Use proper font weights: font-normal, font-medium, font-semibold, font-bold

## Spacing and Layout
- Container: max-w-7xl mx-auto px-6
- Section padding: py-8 or py-12
- Card padding: p-6 or p-8
- Form spacing: space-y-4 or space-y-6
- Grid gaps: gap-4, gap-6, gap-8

## Component Styling Patterns
- Cards: bg-white dark:bg-gray-800 shadow-lg rounded-lg
- Buttons: Use consistent button variants (primary, secondary, outline, ghost)
- Forms: Use consistent form field styling
- Tables: Use proper table styling with hover states
- Modals: Use backdrop blur and proper z-index

## Responsive Design
- Mobile: Default styles (no prefix)
- Tablet: sm: prefix (640px+)
- Desktop: md: prefix (768px+)
- Large: lg: prefix (1024px+)
- Extra Large: xl: prefix (1280px+)

## Animation and Transitions
- Use consistent transition durations (150ms, 300ms)
- Use ease-in-out for smooth transitions
- Include hover states for interactive elements
- Use proper loading states and spinners

## Global Styles
- Defined in [src/app/globals.css](mdc:src/app/globals.css)
- Include custom scrollbar styles
- Use CSS custom properties for theming
- Include proper base styles and resets

## Accessibility
- Ensure proper color contrast ratios
- Use focus states for keyboard navigation
- Include proper ARIA attributes
- Test with screen readers
- Use semantic HTML elements